config PSTORE_SCREEN
	bool "Panic-safe pstore screen common core"
	help
	  Build the allocation-free common text, layout, PSLC, QR and software
	  rendering core used by the Android GKI pstore panic screen. Display,
	  log capture and input providers are added by later integration patches.
	  All panic-time work buffers are supplied by the caller and no external
	  font or userspace service is required.

config PSTORE_SCREEN_DISPLAY
	bool "Panic-safe typed scanout and display-provider registry"
	depends on PSTORE_SCREEN
	help
	  Add the allocation-free typed scanout writer and the stable-sidecar
	  display-provider registry. Providers are prepared in normal context;
	  panic-time reserve, final check, enter, write-span, flush and release
	  callbacks are admitted by independent capability bits and do not acquire
	  DRM modeset locks. Provider descriptors use a versioned known-prefix ABI.

config PSTORE_SCREEN_DRM_SIDECAR
	tristate "DRM stable-sidecar adapter"
	depends on PSTORE_SCREEN_DISPLAY && DRM
	help
	  Validate and pin the description of a driver-owned, linear, single-plane
	  DRM framebuffer whose mapping already exists. The display driver remains
	  responsible for any panic-safe controller switch or cache flush. This
	  does not add fields to DRM public structures and does not infer safety
	  from an arbitrary active GEM buffer. It may be built as a module when
	  the GKI DRM core is modular; provider callback owners remain pinned from
	  normal-context registration through framebuffer, GEM and DRM teardown.
	  Its descriptor also uses a versioned known-prefix ABI and propagates only
	  the callback capabilities explicitly certified by the display driver.

config PSTORE_SCREEN_LOG_CAPTURE
	bool "Frozen panic kmsg tail"
	depends on PSTORE_SCREEN && PRINTK
	depends on LOG_BUF_SHIFT >= 19
	default n
	help
	  Register a built-in panic kmsg dumper which consumes the 5.10 core's
	  preinitialized sequence window with the private non-exported nolock line
	  reader. It retains the exact final 256 KiB of canonical syslog-formatted
	  text even when PSTORE is disabled. The printk dynamic ring must activate
	  with at least 524288 descriptors; allocation failure leaves capture
	  unavailable. No ramoops address is inferred or required.

config PSTORE_SCREEN_PSTORE_MIRROR
	bool "Mirror existing pstore records for the panic screen"
	depends on PSTORE_SCREEN_LOG_CAPTURE && PSTORE
	default y
	help
	  Copy existing pstore records only from normal context after decompression
	  and ECC handling. The panic path consumes a preallocated frozen mirror and
	  never traverses pstore, VFS or backend storage.

config PSTORE_SCREEN_PANIC
	bool "Panic screen orchestration and panic-safe key state machine"
	depends on PSTORE_SCREEN_DISPLAY && PSTORE_SCREEN_LOG_CAPTURE
	default n
	help
	  Enter the selected display provider after the panic kmsg dumper has
	  published its immutable PSLC snapshot. The built-in renderer shows the
	  fixed yellow title, a text projection and raw-byte PSQ1 QR pages. A
	  pre-certified poller may override the weak key and power callbacks; the
	  panic path never calls input core, regmap, VFS, DRM modeset locks or
	  automatic reboot. Single power clicks are committed only after the
	  aggregation window, double clicks are inert, triple clicks request
	  poweroff, long press requests restart, and volume keys page text or QR.
